In the diagram $\overrightarrow{ST}=\underset{\sim}{u}$ and $\overrightarrow{TU}=\underset{\sim}{v}$. Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{SU}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0.6);
\coordinate (T) at (2.6,2.0);
\coordinate (U) at (4.4,0.2);
\draw[->,thick] (S) -- (T) node[midway,above left] {$\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[->,thick] (T) -- (U) node[midway,above right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\node[left] at (S) {$S$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[right] at (U) {$U$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{OA}=\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}=\underset{\sim}{b}$. Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{BA}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.2,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0.2);
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (A) node[midway,above left] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $\overrightarrow{AB}=\underset{\sim}{p}$, $\overrightarrow{BC}=\underset{\sim}{q}$ and $\overrightarrow{CD}=\underset{\sim}{r}$. Which expression equals $\overrightarrow{AD}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.4,1.2);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,0.4);
\coordinate (D) at (5.0,2.6);
\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,above left] {$\underset{\sim}{p}$};
\draw[->,thick] (B) -- (C) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{q}$};
\draw[->,thick] (C) -- (D) node[midway,right] {$\underset{\sim}{r}$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above right] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$M$, $N$ and $P$ are three points, as shown. Which single vector equals $\overrightarrow{MN}-\overrightarrow{PN}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (M) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N) at (3.4,0.8);
\coordinate (P) at (1.6,2.8);
\draw[->,thick] (M) -- (N);
\draw[->,thick] (P) -- (N);
\node[below left] at (M) {$M$};
\node[right] at (N) {$N$};
\node[above] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$RSTU$ is a quadrilateral and $\overrightarrow{RS}+\overrightarrow{ST}+\overrightarrow{TU}=\begin{pmatrix}-3\\8\end{pmatrix}$. Find $\overrightarrow{UR}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\coordinate (R) at (0,0);
\coordinate (S) at (2.8,-0.8);
\coordinate (T) at (4.6,1.2);
\coordinate (U) at (1.8,2.8);
\draw[->,thick] (R) -- (S);
\draw[->,thick] (S) -- (T);
\draw[->,thick] (T) -- (U);
\node[left] at (R) {$R$};
\node[below] at (S) {$S$};
\node[right] at (T) {$T$};
\node[above] at (U) {$U$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
